# A1: the AUDITED eight-seat 262k attach on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-hostgap-2-audit (the timed control's profile plus the host-gap levers - the two-block pre-stage with per-block epochs, the window validate skip, the entry diet - and
# the full read-back audit: after every verify-time diff write EVERY staging destination is read back from every chip and compared with the full-stage value, then the round is staged in full anyway).
# The smoke runs concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix: the quad-blocks smoke rule needs it) and concurrent8_code_32k. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) the attach: 'verify prestage two-block engaged' once for
# each of the two blocks (mode=blocks), 'verify prestage block epochs engaged blocks=2', and NO 'two-block refused' or 'block epochs refused' line; (2) ZERO [PACKED-PRESTAGE-FULLAUDIT] mismatches, read apart by path (a path=full mismatch is the comparator's artifact: the full stage read back against itself; a path=diff mismatch is the lever),
# a path=diff line for block A and for block B, at least one path=full line, buffers x chips checked on every line, and [PACKED-PRESTAGE-SHADOW] lines (the skipped binding check of 1c run as a shadow); (3) c2_smoke_check clean (its hostgap rules: at least 95% of both blocks' 4-live verifies on path=diff, every full stage but the six external-writer reasons counted as a miss, exactly two quad markers,
# a both-quads round); (4) every answer's content hash equal to the control's in S0c (the same prompts, the same 32k code users): the audit stages in full, so equality here proves the staged bytes, and the H and T jobs' equality proves the unaudited arm.
# Then the stage 0 lines: [PACKED-ENTRY], [PACKED-HOSTGAP-VERIFY], [PACKED-HOSTGAP-SELECT], [PACKED-HOSTGAP-WINDOW] (window_ms against fence_wait_ms: a fence_wait_ms near 0 with a window_ms past the
# quads' device time is a window that overran, charged against the lever) and any '[PINDIAG] gc' line (a collection over 5 ms). Duration (estimate): 150 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/hostgap eight-seat host-gap window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/hostgap and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-hostgap-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/hostgap commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-hostgap-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-hostgap-2-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k
